{%- comment -%}
  Section: ds-lp-ergonomic-office-chairs
  Purpose: Ergonomic Office Chairs commercial-hub landing page — BBI Design System v2.
           Answer-first hub for "ergonomic office chair canada". LINKS OUT to the ergonomic
           category hub, the ergoCentric brand page, and the ergonomic comparison blog posts;
           it never re-argues "worth it", mesh-vs-upholstered, or task-vs-executive.
  Used by: page.ergonomic-office-chairs.json (handle: ergonomic-office-chairs)
  Sections: nav → breadcrumbs → hero → intro (answer-first) → differentiators → spec proof
            (VERIFIED Global/OTG specs) → brand lines (company-level) → cross-link tiles →
            entity/OECM note → FAQ → CTA closer → footer → entity JSON-LD.
  JSON-LD: bbi-org-schema is emitted by bbi-nav (NOT re-emitted here). After the footer this page
           emits bbi-service-jsonld + bbi-faq-jsonld (provider/@id → …/#organization).
  FAQ:     Merchant-editable `faq_item` blocks. The visible .lp-faq accordion AND the faq_items list
           passed to bbi-faq-jsonld are built from the SAME blocks (question + "||" + answer, plain
           text, no divergent transforms) so the schema text byte-matches the on-page Q/A
           (SCHEMA-CRIT-1). Block copy must never contain "||" or the "~~~" entry delimiter.
  Specs:   No-assumed-specs — every figure in the Spec Proof grid is cited to data/specs.json
           (Robust GLB74475, Raven OTG10703B, Format MVL3192, Arlo MVL13085) and Roma 1900 series.
           Carrier gate: only carried brands are named; ergoCentric / Keilhauer / Humanscale are
           company-level only (not in data/specs.json — zero spec claims).
  Notes:   Canadian-made / since-1964 copy carries the maple-leaf accent (.bbi-icon--leaf), per the
           BBI brand rule. Reuses the .lp-* vocabulary from ds-lp-sit-stand-desks — no new tokens.
{%- endcomment -%}

